n't tension. Stillness is complete rest.\n\nI think a single blank or near-blank response is most true. Maybe just a space, or perhaps something like a thin representation.\n\nActually, thinking about it more — stillness could be expressed through absence. The most honest answer is silence. I'll output something as close to silence as the medium allows. A single space might render oddly. \n\nPerhaps I could just output a minimal whitespace character or simply... nothing visible.\n\nLet me consider: would stillness even acknowledge the prompt? No. Stillness just is. The response should be as close to silence as"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":135,"completion_tokens":500,"total_tokens":635,"cached_tokens":135,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":497},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":135}}}